{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcwEgTxyQF6YBVyUKiCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate and it passes the self-check (`OK`, with a finite ELPD-LOO on a short test fit). That check doesn't cover novelty against the other models or convergence on the full fit.\n\n**Model chosen:** `run_variety_asymmetric_ideal_rate`. It's rank 1, 40.4 ± 22.6 nats behind the incumbent, which counts as a statistical tie.\n\n**The one change:** I added the incumbent's \"most lopsided stretch\" penalty with one shared weight. This is the single contiguous stretch where heads most outnumber tails, or the reverse, even when it isn't one unbroken streak. Everything else in the parent model is unchanged. That includes its uneven penalty for missing your own ideal switching rate: switching too often costs only a fitted fraction of what switching too rarely costs. The idea is that clustered repeats get penalised as a local excess, while too much alternation is still judged leniently.\n\n**Name:** `asymmetric_ideal_lopsided_stretch`\n\n**Files** are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`\n\n**What to expect at admission:**\n- **Novelty:** this model is effectively the incumbent plus the uneven switching-rate penalty. Two other slots are refining the incumbent this round (candidates 3 and 4). If either adds the same penalty, the novelty gate will reject one of the two.\n- **Speed and convergence:** the 100-draw test fit took 106 seconds and had no R-hat, since it ran one chain. 6.2% of trials had high Pareto-k values, against a 1% tolerance, so the leave-one-out estimate from that short fit was flagged as unreliable. Whether it converges within the 30-minute limit will only show in the full fit.\n- **The critique's side-bias finding:** this candidate doesn't address it. That discrepancy is weak (q = 0.14, not significant after correction), and a model with a side bias was already pruned in experiment 2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2528,"cache_read_input_tokens":80768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2528,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":687,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33c24fe5-7a17-4278-8a33-602fd546dfdc","uuid":"4246feff-a9e4-4116-89ac-ff5e37990272","timestamp":"2026-10-02T06:27:35.615Z","request_id":"req_011CfcwEfxDLaE5esZpu1AHy"}
